==Icelandic==
{{wikipedia|lang=is}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|drykkr||a drink}} from the {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*drunkiz}}, whence also Old English {{m|ang|drync}} and Old High German {{m|goh|trunch}}. Cognate with the Danish {{m|da|drink}} and Swedish {{m|sv|dryck}}.

===Noun===
{{is-noun|m|drykkjar|drykkir}}

# a [[drink]], a [[beverage]]; {{gloss|a served beverage}}
# an [[alcoholic]] [[drink]]; {{gloss|a served alcoholic beverage}}

